From a2c8c76ac81187985cb58bfc9c667e5f6a055b4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:19:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][VideoPlayer] Subtitles in the black bars

Projector users ask for subtitles that never cover the picture of a film wider
than the screen. Kodi places subtitles by the picture it is given: with the bars
of a 2.39:1 film inside a 16:9 picture, as in most UHD remuxes, "Bottom of video"
and "Bottom of screen" are the same place, and two lines reach into the picture.
Kodi does not know those bars.

A setting of Player > Subtitles, "Subtitles in the black bars"
(subtitles.hadesinbars), off by default: subtitles go into the bar under the
picture (VideoRenderers/SubtitleBars.h).

- The bar: from the active area of a Dolby Vision video of its own (level 5),
  where it leaves bars (an area of the whole picture says nothing: many encodes
  write zeros whatever the picture has); otherwise measured on the decoded picture.
  The measurement (SubtitleBarsGLES.cpp) is a pass of its own on the luma plane of
  the picture the renderer is about to draw (VAAPI and software decoding alike, the
  base layer of Dolby Vision included), at most twice a second: per two rows, the
  brightest luma in 16 bands of columns, read back behind a fence at a later
  frame (the thread that draws never waits for the GPU), every piece of GL state it
  touches put back. OpenGL ES 3.0; where it cannot run, it says so once and the
  subtitles stay where Kodi puts them.
- The hysteresis: a bar is taken larger only from measurements that saw the edge
  of the picture lit across (three of them over two seconds at least), so a dark
  scene, a fade or a black picture never moves the subtitles; it is taken smaller
  at once where picture lit across shows inside it (an IMAX scene that opens up);
  a logo or a line burnt into the bar is not picture across it. A level 5 bar that
  a measurement contradicts is not taken again while it lasts.
- The place: the room from the bottom of the active picture to the bottom of the
  screen (with Kodi's own bar under a picture drawn smaller than the screen, a
  3840x1600 encode). Where two lines of text fit with a small gap above and below
  (as libass draws them: font size, line spacing, border and shadow of Kodi's own
  style), the block of two lines is centred in it and one line sits where the
  lower of two would; otherwise subtitles stay where they are (kodi.log says the
  sizes). Picture subtitles (PGS, DVD, DVB): the lowest group of lines goes there
  where it fits, on the same line as two lines would.
- Not moved: Position on screen Manual (the user's own place) and the top, styled
  ASS subtitles with their own places, 3D videos, a menu of a disc. The OSD is
  drawn over subtitles anywhere, as before; with native Dolby Vision, a subtitle
  over a bar takes that edge into the active area sent, as before
  (DVBRIDGE_DV_COVER_HOLD).

The help says the sizes that fit, which the host test asserts: two lines at
Kodi's default size 42 need 146 px of a 1080 frame, more than the 138 px of the
bar of a 2.39:1 film on a 16:9 screen; 38 or less fits it, 34 or less that of a
2.35:1 one.

Strings: core #62450 and #62451, translated in Estuary #54450 and #54451 (en_gb,
es_es, es_ar, es_mx). Tests in tools/regress of LibreELEC: the logic on the host,
and the measurement on Mesa's software GPU.
